  "question": {
    "text": "In an experiment a convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed coaxially on an optical bench in front of a convex mirror at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from it. It is found that an object and its image coincide, if the object is placed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the lens. The focal length of the convex mirror is-"
